-- fold(f) and scan(f) admit every compatible operator and registered reducer (A13): fold(+) is valid and names the same descriptor as +/. Subtraction is admitted exactly because execution is the ordered left recurrence, and drain is a registered step with no declared laws, so exact left order is the only strategy the registry can prove — regrouping is refused, and 12 5 0 0 is the one admissible carry.
-- The fold is the last element of its own scan, for the operator and the registered step alike.
--! registry ../registries/029-ordered-steps.reg

--! out 58
fold(+) Damage @ Enemies

--! out 58
+/ Damage @ Enemies

--! out -34
-/ Damage @ Enemies

--! out 12 5 0 0
drain\ Damage @ Enemies

--! out 0
drain/ Damage @ Enemies

--! out 30
fold(threat) Damage @ Enemies

--! out 12 12 30 30
threat\ Damage @ Enemies
